.TH CLIP 1 "November 2025" "clip 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clip \- copy data to the X clipboard using xclip
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clip
.RI [ file ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B clip
script reads data either from the specified file(s) or from standard input and copies it to the X clipboard using the
.B xclip
utility. It first checks that
.B xclip
is installed; if not, it exits with an error message.

If a filename is provided and the file exists, its contents are sent to
.B xclip
. If no arguments are given, the script reads from standard input (when data is piped in). If neither a file nor piped data is provided, it prints an error and exits with status 1.
.SH OPTIONS
None. The script determines its behavior based on the presence of arguments and whether standard input is a terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Copy the contents of a file to the clipboard:
.nf
$ clip myfile.txt
.fi
.TP
Pipe command output to the clipboard:
.nf
$ ls -l | clip
.fi
.TP
Copy multiple files (concatenated) to the clipboard:
.nf
$ clip file1.txt file2.txt
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Successful copy to clipboard.
.TP
1
Error (e.g., xclip not found, file not found, or no data provided).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xclip (1),
.BR xsel (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by the clip script author.
